      "content": "Yes, potassium is one of the three primary nutrients. The correct answer is A. Potassium.\n\n### 📖 Formula Breakdown (How It Works):\n* **The Formula:** $\\text{Primary nutrients} = \\{\\text{N, P, K}\\}$\n* **What the letters mean:**\n  * $\\text{N}$: Nitrogen – helps with leaf and stem growth.\n  * $\\text{P}$: Phosphorus – helps with root development and flowering.\n  * $\\text{K}$: Potassium – helps with overall plant health and disease resistance.\n* **Why we use it:** Plants need these three elements in the largest quantities, so they are called primary nutrients. Fertilizers are often labeled with their N-P-K ratio.\n\n🎯 **Exam Tip:** Remember that primary nutrients are N, P, K. Sulphur (S) is a secondary nutrient, while oxygen and carbon are not nutrients from soil but are obtained from air and water. Don't confuse potassium (K) with phosphorus (P) – both are primary but different elements."
